## Suggested path (simplest sustainable route)
- **Group A — fix in code (8):** add the `share_properties` block to the 4 resources above. `terraform plan` → in-place update only (no replacement). Apply to dev, then prod.
- **Group B — fix the bootstrap, then backfill (6):**
  - Add the `az ... file-service-properties update --versions SMB3.1.1` step to `createStorageBackend.ts` after account create → future backends compliant.
  - Run that command once for each of the 6 existing backend accounts.
- **Group C — backfill + decide ownership (6):**
  - Run the same `az ... update --versions SMB3.1.1` once per account.
  - Confirm what `normainstorage` and `stwinvm*` are for. If live, bring under Terraform so they don't drift; if unused, flag for deletion (separate decision).
- **Verify:** re-run the Vanta Azure sync → test should flip to 20/20 passing.

## Sustainability principle
Prefer Terraform for anything long-lived (Group A is the model). The `az` one-shots in B/C are the bridge for accounts that live outside IaC today — the durable end-state is getting B and C under Terraform/script control so this can never regress.
